# NSG — beamforming model, control-plane realism, and which KPM families the
# engine collects.
#
# Two of these are HONESTY knobs rather than performance ones. The engine's
# defaults quietly flatter it, and neither was reachable.
#
# ── WIRED ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# * settings.beamforming_model -> MmWaveHelper::BeamformingModel.
#   The default MmWaveSvdBeamforming solves for the BEST POSSIBLE beam from
#   perfect channel knowledge — an upper bound, not a product. MmWaveDftBeamforming
#   steers from a DFT grid and MmWaveCodebookBeamforming is restricted to a
#   finite codebook, which is what real hardware does. MEASURED: SVD 14.53 ->
#   DFT 11.11 Mbps/UE, -23.5%. That gap is roughly the optimism in every number
#   this project has produced so far.
# * settings.use_ideal_rrc -> MmWaveHelper::UseIdealRrc, was hardcoded TRUE.
#   With ideal RRC every attach and handover completes instantly and the control
#   plane costs nothing. Needed a GlobalValue (the scenario Config::SetDefault's
#   it after cmd.Parse). Relevant to the Phase-2b handover work: those handovers
#   were all instantaneous.
# * settings.use_pdsch_for_cqi -> MmWaveHelper::UsePdschForCqiGeneration.
# * settings.rrc_t300_ms -> LteUeRrc::T300 (RRC setup timeout). Note the ns-3
#   time syntax: `+250ms`.
# * settings.kpm_report_du / kpm_report_cu_up / kpm_report_cu_cp -> the e2du /
#   e2cuUp / e2cuCp GlobalValues. These decide the MEASUREMENT SURFACE, not the
#   simulation: switching DU off measurably removes DU metrics (3/3 -> 1/3 of
#   DRB.UEThpDl / RRU.PrbUsedDl / L3servingSINR), and the run then reports
#   "partial" BY DESIGN — that is the toggle working, not a fault.
#   e2du and reducedPmValues had been hardcoded in the run scripts' argument
#   line (`--e2du=1 --reducedPmValues=0`); they are now env-driven.
#
# ── NOT SHIPPED: reduced PM values crash the encoder ───────────────────────
# reducedPmValues=true aborts at t=0.127 s with
#   "Error during the encoding of the RIC Indication Message, errno: Bad file
#    descriptor, failed_type indicationMessage-formats"  (kpm-indication.cc:459)
# The reduced PM container builds a message the ASN.1 encoder rejects. The run
# scripts always passed 0, so upstream never exercised the path. No schema
# field — the third time this rule has applied (dead schedulers, data error
# model, now this): a config must not be able to produce a crashed run.
# NSG_KPM_REDUCED still reaches the engine API, and the test asserts the broken
# state so an upstream fix surfaces.
#
# ── Measured (2026-07-26, engines/nsoran/test_beamforming_kpm.py, PASS) ────
# 3 cells, 6 UEs, 50 Mbps/UE, shadowing on, seed 11:
#
#   A  SVD beamforming, ideal RRC     14.53 Mbps/UE  PRB 41.3  DU 3/3
#   B  DFT beamforming                11.11  (-23.5%) PRB 20.3  DU 3/3
#   C  ideal RRC OFF                  16.68          PRB 38.3  DU 3/3
#   D  DU KPM reporting OFF            —             —         DU 1/3  (partial)
#   E  reduced PM values                                       (crashed)
#
# * The DFT drop is the headline: a beam a real radio could form is worth 23.5%
#   less than the optimum the engine hands you by default.
# * Turning ideal RRC off MEASURED HIGHER (16.68 vs 14.53). Do not read that as
#   "real signalling is faster" — the run reaches a different point in the
#   attach sequence within the same wall-clock window, so the comparison is not
#   like-for-like. What is proven is that the switch reaches the engine; its
#   effect on handover latency needs the /sim/run horizon, not a 0.8 s batch.
